median corner error: homography 0.57%  affine 3.42%   success@2%: 72% vs 28%
A camera orbit changes depth across the poster. Perspective division makes opposite edges shrink by different amounts; an affine map preserves parallelism and cannot represent that keystone. A homography models a planar surface under this motion. Texture loss can still make its estimated fit fail.
Viewpoint 0->208, board: mean RGB difference 0.0958, 48321 supported pixels
Viewpoint 0->208, background: mean RGB difference 0.0640, 106046 supported pixels
Camera translation gives different apparent motion to objects at different depths. The board homography aligns its plane; background residuals can contain parallax, lighting changes and registration error. The overlay uses only the board's coverage, so alignment of other depths is unnecessary.
